.nh
.TH "PB-TUNNEL-STOP" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-tunnel-stop - Stop an ephemeral tunnel


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb tunnel stop <preview> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Stop a temporary preview (the ephemeral lifecycle) by its preview ID. A durable tunnel's ID
(tunnel_...) is refused: use pb tunnel pause or pb tunnel delete for those.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for stop

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print the stopped canonical resource as JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--ephemeral\fP[=false]
	use the temporary preview lifecycle

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  pb tunnel stop preview_abc123
  pb tunnel --ephemeral stop preview_abc123
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-tunnel(1)\fP
